Predictive Analytics Using Historical Data

Project Overview

This project uses historical airline passenger data to analyze trends and forecast future passenger numbers using machine learning.

Objective

To build a predictive model that forecasts future airline passenger trends based on historical data.

Dataset

- Dataset: Monthly Airline Passenger Data
- Records: 144 monthly observations
- Period: 1949–1960
- Features: Month and number of passengers

Tools and Technologies

- Python
- Google Colab
- Pandas
- Matplotlib
- Scikit-learn

Methodology

1. Loaded and explored historical passenger data.
2. Checked missing values and duplicate records.
3. Converted the Month column to datetime format.
4. Visualized historical passenger trends.
5. Split the data chronologically into training and testing sets.
6. Trained a Linear Regression model.
7. Improved the model using month-based seasonal features and a quadratic year trend.
8. Evaluated the model using MAE, MSE, and R² Score.
9. Visualized actual vs predicted passenger numbers.
10. Forecasted passenger numbers for the next 12 months.

Model Evaluation

The improved Linear Regression model achieved:

Metric| Value
MAE| 35.59
MSE| 1754.40
R² Score| 0.713

The improved model performed better than the initial model and captured the general trend and seasonal pattern of passenger numbers.

Visualizations

- Historical Airline Passenger Trends
- Actual vs Predicted Airline Passengers
- Future Airline Passenger Forecast

Conclusion

The project demonstrates how historical data can be used for predictive analytics. The improved Linear Regression model captured the general passenger growth trend and seasonal variations, and generated a 12-month forecast.

